.\" kpm(1) - Kubernetes Pods Metrics
.TH KPM 1 "2026-10-16" "kpm v0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kpm \- Kubernetes Pods Metrics (sample CPU/mem, recommend rightsizing)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpm
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpm
is a Go CLI that samples pod CPU and memory metrics into a local
.B SQLite
store and surfaces rightsizing recommendations.
It uses
.B client-go
directly (no
.BR kubectl
binary) once the sampler is implemented.
.PP
Behavior contract:
.B SPECIFICATIONS.md
and roadmap
.BR docs/ROADMAP.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-print\-sample\-config
Print the embedded sample configuration to stdout and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print version and build metadata.
.TP
.B sample
Sample pod CPU/memory into SQLite
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ).
.B sample.interval_seconds: 0
is one-shot;
.B > 0
runs a daemon loop until SIGINT/SIGTERM.
When
.B notifications.enabled
is true, each daemon tick also evaluates threshold rules and fans out to
.B notifications.sinks
(slack / webhook / smtp).
.TP
.B backup
Safe SQLite copy via
.B VACUUM INTO
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-o ).
.TP
.B restore
Install a backup at the store path, or merge only the rows the store is missing.
.TP
.B export
Export samples as
.B csv
or
.B tsv
.RB ( \-\-format ,
.BR \-o ,
.BR \-\-since ,
.BR \-\-until ,
.BR \-\-namespace ,
.BR \-\-pod ,
.BR \-\-workload ).
.TP
.B capacity
Live pod CPU/memory table from the Metrics API.
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ,
.BR \-\-sort ,
.BR \-\-record\-nodes ).
Default grain: one row per pod (sum util / sum request).
.B \-\-record\-nodes
writes node allocatable/request/util into
.B node_snapshots
(schema v4) for offline analyze-local.
.TP
.B recommend
Offline rightsizing from SQLite history (no cluster).
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-format ,
.BR \-\-namespace ,
.BR \-\-workload ,
.BR \-\-record ,
.BR \-\-score ).
Dual grain (workload and pod); exit
.B 3
when no key meets
.BR min_samples .
.B \-\-record
persists advice into the
.B recommendations
table (schema v2).
.B \-\-score
calibrates latest snapshots against later samples (mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-record ).
.TP
.B doctor
Read-only diagnosis of config, store, history coverage and, only with
.BR \-\-live ,
the cluster Metrics API.
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ,
.BR \-\-format ,
.BR \-\-live ).
Reports every check as
.BR ok ,
.BR warn ,
.B fail
or
.B skip
instead of stopping at the first problem; warnings never fail the run.
Opens the store without creating or migrating it. Exit
.B 0
when nothing verifiably broke,
.B 1
for a general failure, and
.B 2
when only the cluster probe failed.
.TP
.B tui
Interactive live heatmap of pod util ratios (Metrics API).
.RB ( \-\-config ,
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ).
Keys: j/k move, Enter owner-template vs pod-live detail (read-only; Esc close),
s sort, m cpu/mem, b request/limit, d delta column, q quit.
Delta joins read-only
.B recommendations
snapshots when the store file exists; otherwise
.BR n/a .
Delta columns compare live requests to the
.B last recommend \-\-record
snapshot only (not to Git/Helm desired settings).
Example:
.B "113% Δcpu -60m Δmem +3Mi"
— hot util vs
.B current
request; CPU request 60m below last advice (see SPECIFICATIONS.md §5.3.1).
Alias:
.BR "capacity \-\-tui" .
.TP
.B notify\-test
Send one synthetic firing alert to all configured
.B notifications.sinks
.RB ( \-\-config ).
Does not sample the cluster or wait for hold duration.
Requires
.B notifications.enabled
and valid sink
.B *_env
variables (fail-closed).
.TP
.B mcp
Run a read-only MCP server over stdio
.RB ( \-\-config ).
Tools:
.BR get_status ,
.BR list_samples ,
.BR summarize_window ,
.BR list_recommendations .
Uses
.B store.path
from the config; does not require the sample daemon.
When the daemon runs with
.B mcp.enabled ,
.B mcp.listen
serves ops
.RB ( /healthz ,
.BR /readyz ,
.BR /metrics )
without auth (also exempt from allowlist/rate limit), plus MCP
.B /sse
(SSE) and
.B /mcp
(streamable HTTP). Bearer via
.B mcp.token_env
(required off-loopback). Optional
.BR mcp.trusted_proxies ,
.BR mcp.allowlist_cidrs ,
and
.B mcp.rate_limit
follow the gghstats HTTP access mold.
.TP
.B serve
Analyze-local HTTP facade
.RB ( \-\-config ,
optional
.BR \-\-kubeconfig ).
Requires
.B mcp.enabled
and/or
.B server.enabled .
Opens
.B store.path
and binds the shared listen
.RB ( server.listen
if set, else
.BR mcp.listen )
with ops probes, optional MCP
.RB ( /sse ,
.BR /mcp ),
optional JSON
.B /api/v1/*
.RB ( status ,
.BR workloads ,
.BR series ,
.BR recommendations ,
.BR live ,
.BR export/patch ),
and optional charts UI at
.B /
(static assets under
.BR /static/ ),
.B without
a Metrics scrape or sample loop
.RB ( sample.interval_seconds
may be
.BR 0 ).
.B /readyz
checks the store only; kube is optional
.RB ( /api/v1/live
returns 503 JSON when unavailable).
Drawer
.B export/patch
is GitOps copy/download only (never applied by kpm).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kubectl-kpm (1),
.I https://github.com/hrodrig/kpm
.SH AUTHOR
Hermes Rodríguez and contributors.
